    "trigger": "First crossed Career Legacy 7000: Y82",
    "text": "Eleven tackles a game, every game, for 236 games.\n\nAbraham Ward Jr plays in the Green Bay secondary, and his stat line reads like a linebacker's. He has made 2,653 tackles and picked off 33 passes along the way. He has never been credited with a sack or a forced fumble. He does not rush the passer and he does not strip the ball. He finds the ball carrier and puts him on the ground, snap after snap, season after season.\n\nThe Packers made him a champion in Y79, when they beat the Chiefs 44-6 in Super Bowl CXXXVIII, and the league named him Defensive Player of the Year. One ring and one award can look like a small haul for a career this long. The tackles tell the rest of the story.\n\nHe crossed into the Hall in Y82 with another full season on his card, and he is still out there adding to the total. Abraham Ward Jr, welcome to the Hall of Fame."
